-an observation interface faces a fundamental constraint: it cannot choose
-different responses for two underlying states of the world if those states
-produce identical observations. Worlds that present the same observation must
-elicit the same response. This requirement of observational uniformity holds
-whether the decision-maker is an abstract algorithm, a physical mechanism, or an
-embedded biological system.
